## Project Overview

**Kangkong Bread** was an eco-conscious culinary enterprise developed as part of our **National Service Training Program (NSTP) Green Bazaar** during our 1st Year at **Quezon City University (San Bartolome Campus)**.

To introduce this innovative, nutrient-dense baked product to the student body and faculty, I conceptualized and designed the official Facebook promotional campaign collateral. The primary objective was to generate immediate product curiosity, establish a clear value proposition, and drive pre-orders ahead of the physical bazaar launch.

---

## Marketing Objectives & Creative Strategy

1. **Appetite Appeal & Organic Freshness**: Paired crisp product photography of the freshly baked loaf with a natural background of lush green leaves, reinforcing the wholesome, vegetable-infused nature of kangkong bread.
2. **Instant Value Communication**: Featured a high-contrast, bold starburst callout displaying the affordable ₱50 price point, engineered specifically to halt fast-scrolling mobile users in Facebook newsfeeds.
3. **Engaging Brand Personality**: Introduced a friendly cartoon kangkong mascot equipped with a megaphone, adding approachable charm and personal appeal to the pre-order call-to-action (CTA).
4. **Structured Information Architecture**: Guided the viewer’s eye seamlessly through a top-to-bottom hierarchy: headline hook → pricing starburst → hero product visual → pre-order banner → campus distribution location.

---

## Design Breakdown & Rationale

- **Typography & Brand Voice**: The headline utilizes an elegant, organic dark olive serif typeface that evokes artisanal bakery craftsmanship, balanced with clean, high-contrast sans-serif body copy for effortless mobile readability.
- **Color Harmony**: A curated palette of botanical greens (`#2D5A27`, `#4A7C2C`), earthy tones, and warm baked-golden crust hues aligns directly with the environmental ethos of the "Green Bazaar".
- **Visual Depth & Geometry**: Utilized a subtle isometric grid pattern combined with diagonal banner geometry to introduce dynamic energy without distracting from the core product photography.
- **Action-Oriented Call-to-Action (CTA)**: Positioned a prominent "PRE-ORDER NOW!" banner alongside campus event details (San Bartolome Campus) to minimize order friction for fellow students.

---

## Results & Professional Takeaways

- Successfully generated early pre-orders and strong viral engagement across university social media groups prior to bazaar day.
- Demonstrated end-to-end promotional collateral execution: uniting product photography, persuasive copywriting, graphic composition, and commercial positioning into a single cohesive social asset.
